{
  "about": "Small talk Ozi answers in the app itself while it is taking shopping (ruling 66, Anthony, 17 October 2026): 'how are you', 'I'm tired', a hello, a goodbye. These are not the private phrase book (that stays on the server); they are the handful of everyday remarks that must never be mistaken for a product, answered warmly and briefly even when the server is slow. Each entry: an id, the words people say ('when'), and short replies taken in turn. {assistant} becomes the assistant's name; no other name is ever written here. 'nudge' is what Ozi says once to a sentence that is clearly not shopping, and 'quietSeconds' how long it then stays quiet for more chatter.",
